# isInteger

- _isInteger(x, ε)_

Answers `true` if the object _x_ is an `Integer`,
else `false`.
This is the type predicate for the `Integer` type.
It is not the predicate to distinguish integer values at real numeric types,
such as `Float` and `Fraction`,
see `isIntegerValuedNumber`.

At `Integer`:

```
>>> 23L.isInteger
true
```

* * *

